      en: "The Tash-Kumyr Hydroelectric Power Station is an important component of the Naryn cascade, located in the eponymous town in the Jalal-Abad Region. With an output of 450 megawatts, it was designed to further harness the downstream water flow from the larger upstream facilities. Construction took place in the 1980s, with the first turbines coming online towards the end of the decade. The plant relies on the steady discharge from Toktogul and Kurpsai, providing a reliable base load for the national power grid. Beyond electricity generation, the station supports the industrial infrastructure of the former mining town of Tash-Kumyr."
