      en: "The Uch-Kurgan Hydroelectric Power Station is the oldest facility in the Naryn cascade, having commenced operations back in 1961. With an installed capacity of 180 megawatts, it was originally built to supply power to the region's rapidly growing industry and adjacent mining operations. As a pioneer project on the Naryn River, it laid the groundwork for the river's systematic hydrological development. Due to the advanced age of its turbines and generators, the power plant is currently undergoing modernization programs designed to boost efficiency and extend the lifespan of its technical infrastructure for coming decades."
